Fixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:

**Problem:** The `pip` package's source code (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`) was missing from your system Python installation. Only the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) remained, so `pip3` would crash with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'` on every invocation.

**Fix:** Ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which reinstalled the full pip package (source code + metadata) into site-packages.

**Verification:** `pip3 --version` now reports `pip 24.3.1`, and a dry-run `pip install requests` confirms packages can be installed successfully.

